x-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:43d8ceb12f2212b137a80e75288898570a467f50ced848b800542ac45f77f64f","file":"preprints/Universal-Tensor-Squares-for-Symmetric-Groups-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":36,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"9600de0f6d2b41288204945724188ef0999a0e7b32368b06312f6f382fd5505c","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Universal-Tensor-Squares-for-Symmetric-Groups-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:43d8ceb12f2212b137a80e75288898570a467f50ced848b800542ac45f77f64f","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Universal-Tensor-Squares-for-Symmetric-Groups-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L36"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:unipotent-squares}\nFor each positive integer $n\\notin\\{2,4,9\\}$, choose a partition\n$\\lambda_n$ supplied by Theorem~\\ref{thm:main}, including its\nfinite-range witnesses. For every prime power $q$, let $U_q^\\lambda$\ndenote the unipotent irreducible complex character of $\\GL_n(\\mathbb F_q)$\nindexed by $\\lambda\\vdash n$. Then\n$U_q^{\\lambda_n}\\otimes U_q^{\\lambda_n}$ contains $U_q^\\nu$\nfor every $\\nu\\vdash n$."}
